  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a large, sustained offset beginning at index 522 (P1 start) with N/E shifting ~+9 to +12 and U dropping ~-7 to -9, persisting through indices 522–570. At index 571 (P2), a sharp reversal occurs: N/E drop ~-11/-6 and U rises ~+7.7 — consistent with return of temporary platform. P3 (572–573) shows similar reversal but is likely part of the same return event; interior points (572–573) do not sustain a new offset, and numerical_tool_evidence identifies only one pulse (571–572) as best candidate. The return is coherent across all axes and aligns with onset-offset symmetry. No independent permanent step is evident inside the interval; motion before/after differs but that’s permissible. Thus only one genuine temporary platform: P1 onset to P2 return (522–571). P3 is redundant and should be dropped.",
